+| 1 `[P2]` | **A declaration attached to every locked version of a name.** Where a lockfile carries several builds of one package, the name-only lookup marked them all as declared by the manifest, even where the declared constraint admits only one. Measured on this repo: `sha2 0.10.9` carried `fathomdb:constraint = "0.11"`, and the second builds of `thiserror` (`2.0.18`, constraint `1`) and `tokenizers` (`0.22.2`, constraint `0.20`) were tagged `direct`. `depth` and `edit_sites` are the two fields Slice 33 decides on, so this corrupted the output the tool exists to produce. | A declaration now attaches only to the builds its constraint admits, per ecosystem comparator (semver for cargo/npm, PEP 440 for pypi). Non-matching builds stay `transitive` with no origin and no constraint. Verified post-fix: `sha2 0.10.9`, `thiserror 2.0.18` and `tokenizers 0.22.2` are all `transitive`/`None`, exactly one constraint-matching `direct` build survives per name, and **0** components document-wide are `direct` with no origin. |
+
+### 16.2 The 24th criterion — why the suite was unfrozen
+
+**`AC-SBOM-24` — no component may carry a `fathomdb:constraint` that its own version does not
+satisfy.** Test: `test_cyclonedx.py::test_no_component_carries_a_constraint_its_version_violates`.
+
+Slice 31's suite was frozen by design, and Slice 32 held that line for every other criterion. This
+one addition was **ruled by the HITL** (steward `seq-168`, `TC-112` option (a)) on evidence produced
+by the fix itself: the Slice-32 mutation sweep established that **M13** (revert to attach-every-
+version) and **M14** (fallback widens) both leave all 23 criteria GREEN. The oracle could not detect
+the defect fix-1 had just closed — codex found it by reading, not by running the suite. For a slice
+whose output feeds Slice 33's surgical/not-surgical call and thence 0.8.22's dependency backlog, a
+permissive oracle on exactly that field propagates into real dependency decisions.
+
+**Bounds observed, and they were narrow:** exactly one criterion, 23 → 24 and no further; no existing
+test modified, relaxed, renamed or deleted (additions only); demonstrated RED against the pre-fix
+code with **M13 and M14 both failing**; GREEN against the fixed code at `24 passed`; reviewed by
+codex §9 like everything else. It is numbered **last** rather than slotted in, on the `AC-SBOM-23`
+precedent (§4), so every existing id keeps its meaning.
+
+### 16.3 What Slice 32 deliberately did NOT do
+
+- **No CI wiring of any kind.** `seq-166` binds: the suite may be wired only when it is GREEN **and**
+  the HITL has approved — both required, neither sufficient. Reaching 24/24 authorizes nothing.
+  `.github/**`, `scripts/agent-test.sh`, `agent-verify.sh`, `check.sh` and every pytest/ruff config
+  are untouched, and `AC-SBOM-19` remains green *because* the wiring is absent.
+- **No dependency bump, no repo manifest or lockfile edit.** The only manifest added is the tool's own
+  `scripts/sbom-survey/pyproject.toml`. The survey remains an input to 0.8.22.
+- **No survey run of record, no findings doc.** That is Slice 33.
+- Governed-surface allowlist byte-identical (`140c0f63…` at both `be759b0f` and the slice head);
+  SCHEMA stays **24**; no AC minted in `dev/acceptance.md`; no `R-20-xx` id (TC-76).
+
+### 16.4 TC-111 — GREEN requires an install nothing in the repo performs
+
+Recorded here because it is a **precondition on Slice 33**, not a wart. The suite is GREEN only when
+the mini-project's declared dependencies are installed; with a bare interpreter it reports
+**16 failed, 7 passed**, `rc=1`, **0 skipped**, every failure tracing to `No module named 'cyclonedx'`.
+That is the *designed* behaviour — `require_external()` fails rather than skips (§5.7), because an
+ungraded criterion is a green that means nothing — but nothing in the repository performs the install.
+
+Reproduction, verbatim:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m venv /tmp/sbom-venv
+/tmp/sbom-venv/bin/pip install '<repo>/scripts/sbom-survey[dev]'
+/tmp/sbom-venv/bin/pip uninstall -y sbom-survey    # the source tree under test must be what runs
+cd <repo> && /tmp/sbom-venv/bin/python -m pytest scripts/sbom-survey/tests -q -rsE
+```
+
+`pip install` of the project leaves `build/` and `*.egg-info/` in the tree; Slice 32 added both to
+`.gitignore` alongside `out/` and `.venv/`, since Slice 33 must install the tool to run it and an
+unreliable `git status` at that moment is a trap.
+
+**TC-97 is not live here, and the check is not the one §7 predicted.** `scripts/sbom-survey/
+pyproject.toml` *is* an ancestor of the tests, so the pytest header now prints
+`configfile: pyproject.toml` — but the file deliberately carries **no** `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`
+table, so `inicfg == {}` and `getini("pythonpath") == []`. `rootdir` is `scripts/sbom-survey`, and
+`src/python/pyproject.toml` is not on the ancestor chain. The presence of a `configfile:` line is
+therefore not the leak §7 warned about; the absence of an `ini_options` table is what keeps it inert,
+and adding one would reintroduce the hazard.
