The implementation mostly satisfies its acceptance suite, but the tier data introduces an overly broad prefix that can silently classify future manifests that should fail loudly.

Review comment:

- [P2] Narrow root package tier rule to exact files — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-32-sbom-code/scripts/sbom-survey/tiers.toml:31-31
  If a future top-level manifest is added under a common `packages/...` directory, this prefix will match it and silently tag it `dev-tooling` instead of raising `UntieredManifestError` for an unclassified manifest. That undermines the documented “no catch-all / loud gap” behavior; split this into exact rules for `package.json` and `package-lock.json` so only the intended root files are covered.
